  "migration_notes": "Orders v2 changes how an order's money, customer and payment state are represented. The REST payload, the gRPC OrderSummary message and the orders table all change in the same release. Float money caused rounding incidents, so money must be integer minor units plus an ISO 4217 currency. Consumers need a stable customer_id, not only a display name, and PENDING was renamed to AWAITING_PAYMENT. Consumers ship tolerant readers that accept v1 and v2 at the same time, and after one week, remove the v1 code paths."
